  "scope_id": "CORRECTIONS-20261026-001",
  "title": "A Fitting-height-2 group is #P-hard with bounded homology and on knot groups",
  "subject": "The complexity of counting homomorphisms from 3-manifold and knot groups into finite solvable groups",
  "conclusion": "Counting homomorphisms from 3-manifold groups with H1 = Z/3, and from knot groups, into UT3(F4) x| C3, a solvable group of Fitting height 2, is #P-hard: the twisted obstruction is one cubic form whose alternating part Borromean moves steer freely, and an edge gadget turns its kernel count into a Potts partition function. So the bounded-homology line is not the Fitting height, and Rowell's 2009 conjecture fails for this group unless #P functions are polynomial-time computable.",
  "authority_class": "proof",
  "significance": [
    "frontier_change"
  ],
